{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":"2026-06-12T17:22:38.718Z","tool_name":"update_topic","tool_id":"update_topic__7f9zivim","parameters":{"summary":"We have researched the style resolution path in src/style/mod.rs. We found that compute_styles_with_viewport traverses all DOM nodes and calls compute_node_style, which in turn calls collect_matched_rules. Currently, for each rule and each node, selectors are serialized and parsed on the fly. We will now define PreparsedRule, implement preparse_rules to serialize and parse selectors exactly once (and flatten media queries), update compute_styles_with_viewport to build this preparsed rules list, and rewrite compute_node_style/collect_matched_rules to use it.","strategic_intent":"Implementing the hoisted selector parsing and serialization in src/style/mod.rs","title":"Implementing Hoisted Rule Matching Optimization"}}
{"type":"tool_result","timestamp":"2026-06-12T17:22:38.774Z","tool_id":"update_topic__7f9zivim","status":"success","output":"## 📂 Topic: **Implementing Hoisted Rule Matching Optimization**\n\n**Summary:**\nWe have researched the style resolution path in src/style/mod.rs. We found that compute_styles_with_viewport traverses all DOM nodes and calls compute_node_style, which in turn calls collect_matched_rules. Currently, for each rule and each node, selectors are serialized and parsed on the fly. We will now define PreparsedRule, implement preparse_rules to serialize and parse selectors exactly once (and flatten media queries), update compute_styles_with_viewport to build this preparsed rules list, and rewrite compute_node_style/collect_matched_rules to use it.\n\n> [!STRATEGY]\n> **Intent:** Implementing the hoisted selector parsing and serialization in src/style/mod.rs"}
